    ],
    "description": "Hemingray Glass Company Set - 2 Pieces\nHemingray 42 (CD 154)\nAqua, Vintage Mid-Century\nThis set features two vintage aqua glass insulators produced by the Hemingray Glass Company, identified by the \"Hemingray-42\" mold mark. The No. 42 model, classified as CD 154 by collectors, was one of the most widely used designs for telephone and telegraph lines across North America during the early-to-mid 20th century. Prized for their deep aqua color and iconic industrial aesthetic, these pieces represent a significant era of American telecommunications history and are staple items for glass insulator collectors.\nPieces Included:\nGlass Insulator, Hemingray 42, Aqua, Beaded Base - minor fleabites on drip points\nGlass Insulator, Hemingray 42, Aqua, Beaded Base - minor fleabites on drip points\nCondition:\nBoth insulators are in good vintage condition with characteristic wear expected from outdoor utility use. The glass retains high clarity and its original vibrant aqua hue. As is common with authentic vintage insulators, there are minor fleabites and small chips along the sharp drip points on the beaded base. No large structural cracks or major damage to the wire grooves or top domes observed.\nPlease Note:\nThis is a pre-owned item being sold\nas-is\n. We do our best to describe items accurately and include research where possible, but we are not experts in every category. Please note that if the title or description states \"Tested\" that we only test to make sure the unit \"\nPOWERS ON\"\n.\nNo further testing takes place unless stated otherwise and items are considered untested.\nPlease remember all items are used and are sold as is, no refunds.If you have questions, please contact us before bidding.\nFor all vintage clothing, please research sizing before placing a bid.\nItems from different time periods may have measurements that differ from today’s standard sizing.\nCustomer Service:\nReach us via the “Contact Us” link above or by calling\n(540) 361-6550\n. Messages are handled Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:00 PM ET, and we strive to respond within 48 hours.",
